{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>I will certainly return.</b> The angel did not announce that he himself would return to him, but he said it in the mission of the Omnipresent — as in ״וַיֹּאמֶר לָהּ מַלְאַךְ ה׳ הַרְבָּה אַרְבֶּה״, and it was not in his power to multiply, but in the mission of the Omnipresent; so too here, he said it to him in the mission of the Omnipresent (Bereshit Rabbah). Elisha said to the Shunammite woman, ״לַמּוֹעֵד הַזֶּה כָּעֵת חַיָּה אַתְּ חֹבֶקֶת בֵּן,״ and she said, ״אַל אֲדֹנִי אִישׁ הָאֱלֹהִים אַל תְּכַזֵּב בְּשִׁפְחָתֶךָ.״ Those angels who announced to Sarah said, ״לַמּוֹעֵד אָשׁוּב״ — Elisha said to her: Those angels, who are alive and enduring forever, said ״לַמּוֹעֵד אָשׁוּב״; but I am flesh and blood — today alive and tomorrow dead — whether alive or whether dead, ״לַמּוֹעֵד הַזֶּה״ etc." "<b>At the living time.</b> At this same time next year. And it was Pesach, and by the next Pesach Isaac was born — therefore it is not read כְּעֵת but כָּעֵת." "<b>At the living time.</b> At this same time, that she shall be alive for you, that you shall all be whole and enduring." "<b>And he was behind him.</b> The doorway was behind the angel."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:16.668953349Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}